{"book":"James","chapter":3,"translation":"KJV","url":"/bible/james/3","verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"My brethren, be not many masters, knowing that we shall receive the greater condemnation.","words":[["My",["G3450"]],["brethren,",["G80"]],["be",["G1096"]],["not",["G3361"]],["many",["G4183"]],["masters,",["G1320"]],["knowing",["G1492"]],["that",["G3754"]],["we shall receive",["G2983"]],["the greater",["G3187"]],["condemnation.",[]]]},{"verse":2,"text":"For in many things we offend all. If any man offend not in word, the same is a perfect man, and able also to bridle the whole body.","words":[["For",["G1063"]],["in many things",["G4183"]],["we offend",["G4417"]],["all.",["G537"]],["If any man",["G1536"]],["offend",["G4417"]],["not",["G3756"]],["in",["G1722"]],["word,",["G3056"]],["the same",["G3778"]],["is a perfect",["G5046"]],["man,",["G435"]],["and able",["G1415"]],["also",["G2532"]],["to bridle",["G5468"]],["the whole",["G3650"]],["body.",[]]]},{"verse":3,"text":"Behold, we put bits in the horses’ mouths, that they may obey us; and we turn about their whole body.","words":[["Behold,",["G2400"]],["we put",["G906"]],["bits",["G5469"]],["in",["G1519"]],["the horses’",["G2462"]],["mouths,",["G4750"]],["that",["G4314"]],["they",["G846"]],["may obey",["G3982"]],["us;",["G2254"]],["and",["G2532"]],["we turn about",["G3329"]],["their",["G846"]],["whole",["G3650"]],["body.",[]]]},{"verse":4,"text":"Behold also the ships, which though they be so great, and are driven of fierce winds, yet are they turned about with a very small helm, whithersoever the governor listeth.","words":[["Behold",["G2400"]],["also",["G2532"]],["the ships,",["G4143"]],["which though they be",["G5607"]],["so great,",["G5082"]],["and",["G2532"]],["are driven",["G1643"]],["of",["G5259"]],["fierce",["G4642"]],["winds,",["G417"]],["yet are they turned about",["G3329"]],["with",["G5259"]],["a very small",["G1646"]],["helm,",["G4079"]],["whithersoever",["G3699","G302"]],["the governor",["G2116"]],["listeth.",["G3730"]]]},{"verse":5,"text":"Even so the tongue is a little member, and boasteth great things. Behold, how great a matter a little fire kindleth!","words":[["Even",["G2532"]],["so",["G3779"]],["the tongue",["G1100"]],["is",["G2076"]],["a little",["G3398"]],["member,",["G3196"]],["and",["G2532"]],["boasteth great things.",["G3166"]],["Behold,",["G2400"]],["how great",["G2245"]],["a matter",["G5208"]],["a little",["G3641"]],["fire",["G4442"]],["kindleth!",[]]]},{"verse":6,"text":"And the tongue is a fire, a world of iniquity: so is the tongue among our members, that it defileth the whole body, and setteth on fire the course of nature; and it is set on fire of hell.","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["the tongue",["G1100"]],["is a fire,",["G4442"]],["a world",["G2889"]],["of iniquity:",["G93"]],["so",["G3779"]],["is",["G2525"]],["the tongue",["G1100"]],["among",["G1722"]],["our",["G2257"]],["members,",["G3196"]],["that it defileth",["G4695"]],["the whole",["G3650"]],["body,",["G4983"]],["and",["G2532"]],["setteth on fire",["G5394"]],["the course",["G5164"]],["of nature;",["G1078"]],["and",["G2532"]],["it is set on fire",["G5394"]],["of",["G5259"]],["hell.",[]]]},{"verse":7,"text":"For every kind of beasts, and of birds, and of serpents, and of things in the sea, is tamed, and hath been tamed of mankind:","words":[["For",["G1063"]],["every",["G3956"]],["kind",["G5449"]],["of beasts,",["G2342"]],["and",["G5037","G2532"]],["of birds,",["G4071"]],["and",["G5037"]],["of serpents,",["G2062"]],["and",["G2532"]],["of things in the sea,",["G1724"]],["is tamed,",["G1150"]],["and",["G2532"]],["hath been tamed",["G1150"]],["of mankind:",["G5449"]]]},{"verse":8,"text":"But the tongue can no man tame; it is an unruly evil, full of deadly poison.","words":[["But",["G1161"]],["the tongue",["G1100"]],["can",["G1410"]],["no",["G3762"]],["man",["G444"]],["tame;",["G1150"]],["it is an unruly",["G183"]],["evil,",["G2556"]],["full",["G3324"]],["of deadly",["G2287"]],["poison.",[]]]},{"verse":9,"text":"Therewith bless we God, even the Father; and therewith curse we men, which are made after the similitude of God.","words":[["Therewith",["G1722","G846"]],["bless we",["G2127"]],["God,",["G2316"]],["even",["G2532"]],["the Father;",["G3962"]],["and",["G2532"]],["therewith",["G1722","G846"]],["curse we",["G2672"]],["men,",["G444"]],["which",["G3588"]],["are made",["G1096"]],["after",["G2596"]],["the similitude",["G3669"]],["of God.",[]]]},{"verse":10,"text":"Out of the same mouth proceedeth blessing and cursing. My brethren, these things ought not so to be.","words":[["Out of",["G1537"]],["the same",["G846"]],["mouth",["G4750"]],["proceedeth",["G1831"]],["blessing",["G2129"]],["and",["G2532"]],["cursing.",["G2671"]],["My",["G3450"]],["brethren,",["G80"]],["these things",["G5023"]],["ought",["G5534"]],["not",["G3756"]],["so",["G3779"]],["to be.",[]]]},{"verse":11,"text":"Doth a fountain send forth at the same place sweet water and bitter?","words":[["Doth",["G3385"]],["a fountain",["G4077"]],["send forth",["G1032"]],["at",["G1537"]],["the same",["G846"]],["place",["G3692"]],["sweet",["G1099"]],["water and",["G2532"]],["bitter?",[]]]},{"verse":12,"text":"Can the fig tree, my brethren, bear olive berries? either a vine, figs? so can no fountain both yield salt water and fresh.","words":[["Can",["G3361","G1410"]],["the fig tree,",["G4808"]],["my",["G3450"]],["brethren,",["G80"]],["bear",["G4160"]],["olive berries?",["G1636"]],["either",["G2228"]],["a vine,",["G288"]],["figs?",["G4810"]],["so",["G3779"]],["can no",["G3762"]],["fountain",["G4077"]],["both yield",["G4160"]],["salt",["G252"]],["water",["G5204"]],["and",["G2532"]],["fresh.",[]]]},{"verse":13,"text":"Who is a wise man and endued with knowledge among you? let him shew out of a good conversation his works with meekness of wisdom.","words":[["Who",["G5101"]],["is a wise man",["G4680"]],["and",["G2532"]],["endued with knowledge",["G1990"]],["among",["G1722"]],["you?",["G5213"]],["let him shew",["G1166"]],["out of",["G1537"]],["a good",["G2570"]],["conversation",["G391"]],["his",["G846"]],["works",["G2041"]],["with",["G1722"]],["meekness",["G4240"]],["of wisdom.",[]]]},{"verse":14,"text":"But if ye have bitter envying and strife in your hearts, glory not, and lie not against the truth.","words":[["But",["G1161"]],["if",["G1487"]],["ye have",["G2192"]],["bitter",["G4089"]],["envying",["G2205"]],["and",["G2532"]],["strife",["G2052"]],["in",["G1722"]],["your",["G5216"]],["hearts,",["G2588"]],["glory",["G2620"]],["not,",["G3361"]],["and",["G2532"]],["lie not",["G5574"]],["against",["G2596"]],["the truth.",[]]]},{"verse":15,"text":"This wisdom descendeth not from above, but is earthly, sensual, devilish.","words":[["This",["G3778"]],["wisdom",["G4678"]],["descendeth",["G2076","G2718"]],["not",["G3756"]],["from above,",["G509"]],["but",["G235"]],["is earthly,",["G1919"]],["sensual,",["G5591"]],["devilish.",[]]]},{"verse":16,"text":"For where envying and strife is, there is confusion and every evil work.","words":[["For",["G1063"]],["where",["G3699"]],["envying",["G2205"]],["and",["G2532"]],["strife",["G2052"]],["is, there",["G1563"]],["is confusion",["G181"]],["and",["G2532"]],["every",["G3956"]],["evil",["G5337"]],["work.",[]]]},{"verse":17,"text":"But the wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceable, gentle, and easy to be intreated, full of mercy and good fruits, without partiality, and without hypocrisy.","words":[["But",["G1161"]],["the wisdom",["G4678"]],["that is from above",["G509"]],["is",["G2076"]],["first",["G4412"]],["pure,",["G3303","G53"]],["then",["G1899"]],["peaceable,",["G1516"]],["gentle,",["G1933"]],["and easy to be intreated,",["G2138"]],["full",["G3324"]],["of mercy",["G1656"]],["and",["G2532"]],["good",["G18"]],["fruits,",["G2590"]],["without partiality,",["G87"]],["and",["G2532"]],["without hypocrisy.",[]]]},{"verse":18,"text":"And the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace of them that make peace.","words":[["And",["G1161"]],["the fruit",["G2590"]],["of righteousness",["G1343"]],["is sown",["G4687"]],["in",["G1722"]],["peace",["G1515"]],["of them that make",["G4160"]],["peace.",[]]]}]}